@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Security audit — 2026-10-30
+
+**Scope.** Whole repository at main `68c6c31` / `b8aabec`, including the finance module (`sql/023`, `sql/024`,
+`apps/api/src/modules/finance/routes.ts`, `apps/web/src/modules/finance/Finance.tsx`): the Worker API (auth, tenancy,
+routes, WhatsApp webhook, outbox job), every migration (RLS, grants, SECURITY DEFINER functions), the web app
+(XSS sinks, token storage, headers), CI/deploy config, committed secrets and dependencies.
+
+**Method.** Code reading plus automated sweeps: per-table RLS / revoke / policy check across all migrations, every
+SECURITY DEFINER function checked for `search_path` and an org/role guard, every function checked for an explicit
+revoke from `public`/`anon`, cross-tenant foreign-ID checks in the create functions, secret patterns over tracked files
+and history, `npm audit` (0 vulnerabilities). No live testing against the API or database.
+
+**Fixes.** Branch `worktree-security-audit-fixes`, migration `sql/025_security_audit_fixes.sql`, test
+`sql/tests/021_security_audit_fixes.sql`. See the worklog entry of 2026-10-30, "Security audit fixes".
+
+## Result
+
+No critical or high findings. Tenant isolation in the database holds: the `X-Org-Id` header is re-checked against
+membership on every call, every business table has RLS with select-only grants, every user-callable function starts with
+a role/org/module guard, and the create functions verify that every referenced row belongs to the caller's organization.
+
+| Severity | Count |
+|---|---|
+| Critical | 0 |
+| High | 0 |
+| Medium | 3 |
+| Low | 5 |
+| Info | 3 |
+
+## Verified as sound
+
+- JWT verified against Supabase JWKS with issuer and audience; WhatsApp `X-Hub-Signature-256` checked in constant time before parsing.
+- `current_org_id()` validates the header as a UUID and checks active membership every call.
+- All tables: RLS on, `revoke all` from `anon`/`authenticated`, select only; no grants to `anon`; no definer function without `search_path`.
+- Read policies match API permissions (members and viewers get every `*.read`; finance is owner/admin in both).
+- `inv_decide_request`: org, role, self-approval and state checked under `for update`; multi-approver counting correct.
+- WhatsApp number binding: random codes stored hashed, 5 tries per code, 5 requests per hour, bound to the caller's own row.
+- No XSS sinks in the web app; no committed secrets; `npm audit` clean.
+
+## Findings and what was done
+
+| ID | Severity | Location | Finding | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| M-1 | Medium | `apps/api/src/modules/core/memberRoutes.ts` | Member list/invite/role/disable ran with the secret key (bypassing RLS), protected only by the Worker's permission check; the audit row was written in a separate call after the change, so a change could exist without its audit row. Broke the "secret key not in request routes" and "audit in the same transaction" rules. | **Fixed.** Database functions `core_list_members`, `core_set_member_role`, `core_set_member_disabled`, `core_add_invited_account` called with the user's own login; rules (own role, owners only by owners, at least one owner, with owner rows locked) and audit in one transaction. The secret key is now only in `lib/authAdmin.ts` for Supabase Auth account calls, after the database has allowed the action. `lib/audit.ts` and `modules/core/members.ts` removed; boundary tests updated. |
+| M-2 | Medium | `memberRoutes.ts` (invite) | An admin of any organization could add any existing account on the platform by email, without consent; the response showed whether the email had an account; the other organization then saw that person's email and last sign-in time. | **Fixed (consent).** Existing accounts get a `core_invitations` row and join only after accepting in the organization picker (`core_my_invitations`, `core_respond_invitation`); admins can withdraw pending invitations. **Remaining:** the inviting admin can still tell whether an email has an account (new accounts return a link to send; existing ones get "invited"). Closing that needs invites sent by email instead of links handed to the admin: a product decision. |
+| M-3 | Medium | `apps/web/public/_headers` | No CSP, HSTS or frame protection while the Supabase session sits in localStorage. | **Fixed.** CSP (`script-src 'self'`, `connect-src` limited to the API and `*.supabase.co`, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, `object-src 'none'`), HSTS, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Permissions-Policy`. Built page checked: no inline script. |
+| L-1 | Low | `apps/api/wrangler.toml`, CI deploy | Production ran with `APP_ENV=development` and `http://localhost:5173` as an allowed origin (also usable as the invite-link redirect). | **Fixed.** `wrangler.toml` holds production values; local values come from the root `.env` (documented in `.dev.vars.example`). |
+| L-2 | Low | `inv_decide_request`, `inv_decide_adjustment` | The caller chose `p_channel`, so a user calling directly could record a decision as `whatsapp` in the audit log. | **Fixed.** A channel other than `app` is accepted only when `msg_decide_by_token` (service role only) vouches for it for that transaction. |
+| L-3 | Low | `msg_decide_by_token`, `msg_task_reply` | Verified numbers are unique per organization, but the lookup ignored the organization; one person verified in two organizations resolved to an arbitrary one. | **Fixed.** Tokens and open tasks are searched across every organization where the number is verified. |
+| L-4 | Low | `/v1/messaging/process`, `jobs/outbox.ts` | Any organization's admin could run delivery and the audit-chain check for all organizations, and saw counts from the others. | **Fixed.** `msg_claim_due_for_org`; the on-demand pass skips the all-org audit check. Rate limiting left to I-3. |
+| L-5 | Low | `memberRoutes.ts` (invite link) | A sign-in link (credential) could be issued for an invited, never-signed-in account even after it joined another organization. | **Fixed.** `core_invite_link_target` refuses if the account belongs to or is invited by another organization, and audits the request. |
+| I-1 | Info | `apps/api/src/index.ts` | WhatsApp verify token compared with `===`. | **Fixed.** `safeEqual` (constant time), with a unit test. |
+| I-2 | Info | `sql/001_tenancy_core.sql` | Stale comment: "The API uses the service-role key". | **Open.** The file is write-protected for agents; comment-only, no effect on the database. |
+| I-3 | Info | API | No request rate limiting (apart from the database limit on code requests). | **Open.** Add a Cloudflare WAF rate-limiting rule on `/v1/*` and `/webhooks/*` (dashboard setting, not code). |
+
+## Also found
+
+- Commits `68c6c31` and `b8aabec` on main added this audit's worktree folder as a gitlink (`.claude/worktrees/security-audit-fixes`).
+  `.gitignore` now ignores `.claude/worktrees/`; untrack it on main with `git rm --cached .claude/worktrees/security-audit-fixes`.
+
+## Before this is live
+
+1. Run `sql/025_security_audit_fixes.sql` on staging, then `sql/tests/021_security_audit_fixes.sql` (expect `ALL TESTS PASSED`), then production. Run it **before** deploying the Worker.
+2. Add `APP_ENV=development` and `ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173` to the root `.env` for local development.
+3. Test by hand: invite an existing account and accept it from the organization picker; invite a new email and use the link; change a role; disable/enable; withdraw an invitation; check the browser console for CSP errors.
